  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive). Pattern: X⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{眠|ねむ}る (X sleeps).\n\nASPECT: ている indicates state of sleeping. {眠|ねむ}っている = 'is asleep.'\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・⟦ぐっすり→ぐっすり：02676_gussuri⟧{眠|ねむ}る (sleep soundly)\n・⟦よく→よく：00601_yoku⟧{眠|ねむ}れる (can sleep well)\n・{眠|ねむ}れない (can't sleep)\n・⟦{眠|ねむ}り→眠り：13673_nemuri⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦つく→就く：10123_tsuku⟧ (fall asleep)\n・⟦{永遠|えいえん}→永遠：01873_eien⟧⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{眠|ねむ}り→眠り：13673_nemuri⟧ (eternal sleep—death euphemism)\n\nCONTRAST WITH ⟦{寝|ね}る→寝る：00470_neru⟧:\n・{眠|ねむ}る: to sleep (the state of being asleep)\n・⟦{寝|ね}る→寝る：00470_neru⟧: to go to bed, to lie down, to sleep (broader meaning)\n\n⟦{寝|ね}る→寝る：00470_neru⟧ is more common in everyday speech and includes 'going to bed.' {眠|ねむ}る specifically means 'to be asleep.'\n\nRELATED:\n・⟦{眠|ねむ}い→眠い：00872_nemui⟧ (sleepy—adjective)\n・⟦{眠|ねむ}り→眠り：13673_nemuri⟧ (sleep—noun)",
